Fix WAL replay dropping jobs at max-job-size (issue #82; upstream bug, unfixed
in v1.13 and on master).

put accepts a body of up to job_data_size_limit bytes and stores the job with
body_size + 2, the body plus its trailing CRLF. readrec() and readrec5()
compared that stored size against job_data_size_limit itself, so on restart a
job whose body was max-job-size or max-job-size - 1 bytes was reported as
"too big", and the Error path stopped reading the rest of that binlog file,
dropping every later job in it.

Allow for the CRLF in the replay check. A stored record larger than a legal
put could have written is still rejected. The record format is unchanged, so
binlogs written before this fix replay correctly.

--- a/file.c
+++ b/file.c
@@ -223,7 +223,9 @@
     case Buried:
     case Delayed:
         if (!j) {
-            if ((size_t)jr.body_size > job_data_size_limit) {
+            /* body_size includes the trailing CRLF that put stores after a
+             * body of up to job_data_size_limit bytes. */
+            if ((size_t)jr.body_size > job_data_size_limit + 2) {
                 warnpos(f, -r, "job %"PRIu64" is too big (%"PRId32" > %zu)",
                         jr.id,
                         jr.body_size,
@@ -348,7 +350,9 @@
     case Buried:
     case Delayed:
